  "note": "Annual election of the Antrim Town Commissioners, polled Friday 15 May 1936 (the January 1935 round having been deferred by the Local Government Act (Northern Ireland) 1934). The nine retiring members were again nominated and no contest took place (Belfast News-Letter, 7 May 1936, p. 10). Exactly the nine retiring members; 'Begg' appears in the OCR as 'Begun', normalised against the 1932 and 1939 lists. Returned unopposed."
